From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kierandrewett <kieran@drewett.dev>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 17:15:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] build: accept the schema and IBus releases of Debian 13

Debian 13 ships gsettings-desktop-schemas 48.0 and IBus 1.5.32.

The schema headers of 48.0 have every enum value that the code uses.
The input settings that later schemas added (scroll speed, the
disable-while-typing timeout, custom acceleration, scroll wheel
emulation, the eraser button) are read only when the installed schema
has the key, so with 48.0 they can be set only in the Gnoblin Lua
configuration.

With IBus 1.5.32 the Gnoblin IBus input method keeps working. It shows
the preedit text without the per-segment hints that IBus 1.5.33 added.
Without this change the build silently left the IBus input method out.

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
index 00bfb4221..7a8e29cb8 100644
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@ pango_req = '>= 1.46.0'
 cairo_req = '>= 1.10.0'
 pangocairo_req = '>= 1.20'
 pixman_req = '>= 0.42'
-gsettings_desktop_schemas_req = '>= 49.1'
+gsettings_desktop_schemas_req = '>= 48.0'
 x11_req = '>= 1.7.0'
 xcomposite_req = '>= 0.4'
 xkbcommon_req = '>= 0.4.3'
@@ -122,7 +122,7 @@ hyprcursor_dep = dependency('hyprcursor', version: '>= 0.1.11', required: get_op
 have_hyprcursor = hyprcursor_dep.found()
 if have_hyprcursor
 endif
-ibus_dep = dependency('ibus-1.0', version: '>= 1.5.33', required: get_option('ibus'))
+ibus_dep = dependency('ibus-1.0', version: '>= 1.5.32', required: get_option('ibus'))
 have_ibus = ibus_dep.found()
 pixman_dep = dependency('pixman-1', version: pixman_req)
 gsettings_desktop_schemas_dep = dependency('gsettings-desktop-schemas',
